[00:00.00] 作词 : Morgan Wallen/Ernest Keith Smith/Ryan Vojtesak/Michael Hardy/James Maddocks
[00:00.00][by:一只叫波罗的猫]
[00:01.00] 作曲 : Morgan Wallen/Ernest Keith Smith/Ryan Vojtesak/Michael Hardy/James Maddocks
[00:14.57]Hey, Mister City Man
[00:14.57]嘿 都市先生
[00:17.15]Rollie on your wrist, Nasdaq in your hand
[00:17.15]腕间戴着劳力士 手中操盘纳斯达克
[00:20.39]Rollin' your eyes at my beat-up truck
[00:20.39]对我破旧的卡车翻白眼
[00:23.51]Feed in the back, spittin' in my cup
[00:23.51]后座堆满饲料 往我杯子里吐口水
[00:27.44]Both our tags say Tennessee
[00:27.44]我们的车牌都写着田纳西
[00:29.74]I don't know you, I know you don't know me
[00:29.74]你不认识我 我也知道你不在意
[00:32.86]But if this red light didn't have to change
[00:32.86]若这红灯永远不会变绿
[00:36.65]I'd have time to say
[00:36.65]我才有时间告诉你
[00:38.89]When you die, I hope you come back as a redneck
[00:38.89]愿你下辈子投胎做个红脖儿
[00:45.26]I hope it sticks on you like a hell-hot sun tattoo
[00:45.26]让烈日般的刺青 永远刻在你身上
[00:51.68]I hope you break your back for that barely-get-by paycheck
[00:51.68]愿你为微薄的薪水累弯脊梁
[00:58.03]And when you can't, you gotta go and bloody up a buck or two
[00:58.03]走投无路时 不得不猎杀野鹿换口粮
[01:05.05]Catch the Holy Ghost on a pinewood bench
[01:05.05]在松木长椅上感受圣灵降临
[01:08.32]Drive across the county just to hook up a winch
[01:08.32]横跨整个郡 只为安装一个绞盘
[01:11.54]Revel in the pride of a simple man
[01:11.54]为身为普通人而骄傲
[01:15.37]Maybe then you'll understand
[01:15.37]或许那时你才会懂
[01:24.27]Oh
[01:24.27]噢
[01:30.46]I didn't choose my raisin' and you didn't choose yours
[01:30.46]我们都无法选择出身
[01:33.86]You work in four walls and I'm workin' four-by-fours
[01:33.86]你困在四面墙内工作 我与四驱车为伴
[01:37.62]We ain't as different as you think we is, but I didn't pull up sayin'
[01:37.62]我们并非如你想的那般不同 但我不会像你那样
[01:42.53]"Won't you look at that born rich, fed with a silver spoon, trust fund kid," like you did
[01:42.53]指着我说 看看这些 生来贫穷的乡巴佬
[01:49.07]So when you die, I hope you come back as a redneck
[01:49.07]所以愿你下辈子投胎做个红脖儿
[01:55.45]I hope it sticks on you like a hell-hot sun tattoo
[01:55.45]让烈日般的印记 永远刻在你皮肤
[02:01.99]I hope you break your back for that barely-get-by paycheck
[02:01.99]愿你为勉强糊口的工资拼尽全力
[02:08.35]And when you can't, you gotta go and bloody up a buck or two
[02:08.35]撑不下去时 只能用猎枪换生存的希望
[02:15.63]Catch the Holy Ghost on a pinewood bench
[02:15.63]在乡间木凳上遇见信仰的光
[02:18.70]Drive across the county just to hook up a winch
[02:18.70]穿越田野去修理生锈的绞车
[02:21.84]Revel in the pride of a simple man
[02:21.84]以平凡人的坚韧为荣光
[02:25.64]Maybe then you'll understand
[02:25.64]或许那时你才会懂
[02:29.02]Why we say grace, why we hold hands
[02:29.02]为何我们餐前祈祷 为何我们手牵手
[02:32.23]Keep a shotgun right by the nightstand
[02:32.23]床头柜永远放着猎枪
[02:35.20]And why we love a good rain comin' down
[02:35.20]为何我们热爱暴雨倾盆的时刻
[02:38.00]And never leave these so-called backward, backwood, good-for-nothing, hillbilly hick towns
[02:38.00]为何死守这被嘲笑的落后山村 永不离开
[02:46.77]So when you die, I hope you come back as a redneck
[02:46.77]所以愿你下辈子投胎做个红脖儿
[02:53.26]I hope it sticks on you like a hell-hot sun tattoo
[02:53.26]让南方的烈日 在你身上留下烙印
[02:59.59]I hope you break your back for that barely-get-by paycheck
[02:59.59]愿你体会为生活弯腰的滋味
[03:06.04]And when you can't, you gotta go and bloody up a buck or two, yes, you do
[03:06.04]走投无路时 懂得用双手换取生存的权利
[03:13.07]Catch the Holy Ghost on a pinewood bench
[03:13.07]在松木长椅上找到内心的宁静
[03:16.32]Drive across the county just to hook up a winch
[03:16.32]为了生活奔波却依然骄傲
[03:19.55]Revel in the pride of a simple man
[03:19.55]以最朴素的方式活着 并为之自豪
[03:23.32]Maybe then you'll understand
[03:23.32]或许那时你才会懂
[03:32.18]Oh
[03:32.18]噢
[03:36.83]Yeah, then you'll understand
[03:36.83]是的 那时你才会懂
